      "content": "Risk and reward must remain nonnegative once their boundaries are crossed (A41). For example, 100 shares with Stop 47.50 and Mark 47.00 currently return risk −$50; a Mark above the Target similarly returns negative incremental reward. Floor both distances at zero and add boundary-crossing tests; any excess belongs in separate Overrun figures.",
